    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0626" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4593: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Switzerland
                        (Wilson), at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-06T15:00:00-05:00">March 6, 1932—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Your 56, March 6, 11 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>If the Chinese authorities with whom our Minister at Shanghai is to
                        consult in regard to agenda are the highest national Chinese authorities, I
                        feel that my No. 28, March 5, 9 p.m. to you and my instruction to Minister
                        Johnson of March 5, 9 p.m.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d559-f1"/> the text of
                        which was communicated to you in my No. 29, March 5, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="54"
                            xml:id="d559-f2"/> sufficiently indicate my views in regard to the
                        points raised in your telegrams 54 and 56.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It would seem important to get the representatives of the various powers
                        most concerned into conference at Shanghai at the earliest possible
                        moment.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d559-f1" n="53" xml:id="d559-f1-content">
                <p>For Department’s instruction, see telegram No. 77 to the Consul General at
                    Shanghai, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_209"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 209</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d559-f2" n="54" xml:id="d559-f2-content">
                <p>No. 29 not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
